<in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock contextRef="OneD">Notes:  n  n1. The above consolidated unaudited financial results for the quarter and nine months ended 31st  n December 2020 were reviewed by the Audit Committee vide its meeting held on 10th February 2021   nand then approved by the Board of Directors at its meeting held on 11th February 2021.The Statutory   nAuditors of the company have conducted a  Limited Review  of the above consolidated unaudited  n financial results.  n  n2.  The  consolidated unaudited financial results for the quarter and nine months ended 31st December 2020  n have been prepared in accordance with Indian Accounting Standards ( Ind AS ) as prescribed under   nSection 133 of the Companies Act, 2013 read with relevant rules thereunder and in terms of Regulation   n33 of the SEBI (Listing Obligations and Disclosure Requirements) Regulation, 2015.  n  n3.  The consolidated financial results include the financial results of Indo National Limited and the financial   nresults of its subsidiary M/s Helios Strategic Systems Limited and step down subsidiaries, M/s Kineco   nlimited , Kineco Kaman Composites -India Private Limited and Kineco Alte Train Technologies Pvt Ltd   n  n4.  For the quarter ended 31st December 2020, one of the step down subsidiary M/s.Kineco Ltd has  n achieved the revenue of Rs. 108.19 Crores, which amounts to more than 10% of the total consolidated  nrevenue of Rs. 403.14 crores.  M/s.Kineco Ltd and its subsidiaries is in the business segment of   nComposites and Aerospaces. Considering the same and in accordance with IND AS 108,  segment  n reporting  becomes applicable for consolidated financial statements and the same is being given  n herewith.  n  n5. The full impact of COVID19 still remains uncertain and could be different from our estimates when we  n prepared these financial results. The Company will continue to closely monitor any material changes to  nfuture economic conditions.  n  n6.  The Central Government has published the Code on Social Security, 2020 and Industrial Relations Code,  n2020 ( the codes ) in the Gazette of India, interalia, subsuming various existing labour and industrial laws  n which deals with employees including post employment period. The Ministry of labour and employment  n has released draft rules for the Code on Social Security 2020 on November 13, 2020 which are yet to be  n notified. The company will assess and evaluate the impact once the subject rules are notified and will  nappropriately consider the same in its financial statements in the period in which the Code becomes  n effective.  n  n7. Previous year/period's figures have been regrouped, wherever necessary, to conform to the current year  n/period's classification / disclosure</in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock>
